license-url: "https://github.com/HOOOnsssy/LC50-prediction-with-FiLM-Concatenation-fusion/blob/HEAD/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  Model definitions, inference and numerical interpretation code, input data,
  and trained checkpoints for aquatic LC50 prediction. The release contains
  twelve encoder-fusion configurations across ten compound-level splits and
  thirty auxiliary checkpoints. Original code and checkpoints are provided
  under a custom non-commercial academic research license. Source data have
  separate terms described in DATA_NOTICE.md.
keywords:
  - aquatic toxicity
  - LC50
  - graph neural networks
  - FiLM
  - multimodal learning
references:
